{"item": "videorft_incentivizing_video_reasoning_c::97", "novel": false, "evidence": "MUSEG: Reinforcing Video Temporal Understanding via Timestamp-Aware Multi-Segment Grounding", "evidence_levels": [1, 2], "justification": "MUSEG and TempR1 together substantially cover the core contributions: RL-based fine-tuning with timestamp-aware grounding rewards to improve fine-grained temporal understanding in MLLMs, which is the central problem and approach of TemporalRFT. While TemporalRFT adds a causal ordering reward and a lightweight temporal attention module, these are incremental additions that do not constitute a sufficiently distinct core contribution given that the fundamental paradigm (RFT + timestamp-grounded rewards for temporal localization) is already established.", "checked": 1, "candidates": ["44d46ed197aedcf2344f0b77250cbd6211c9c0a8", "ec3456950811ceb0bcb97601af57f812ece01744", "fdb0219b1e3daa0e8a29d11ca2e2951353e6283b", "a3cdf5d2d5c53370dd6173b509438481e32a0419", "ac8089bb7944090cf1de5df25aadf5e6356f3040", "d905973335615ae99024fb3aeedd0e4ec94a5606", "387eb5c690c5b4dd28a4a7e725788a992e45d152", "e9689a588715666c1630ba58f96318480610e82a", "5de5e469f3d27980c8e5407f5bd1107041cfd498", "0af4359948693c7aa60caf5e13aaab9d32fced92", "b368528a18d8f7b377e6fc74c1050df8c0348a1f", "ee8c1a46c90f1261c23479e15c6bed7f67ad8943", "6e5d44204a19a673efa245858c3ea41f45d0723f"], "B_id": null, "B_rank": null, "new_calls": 7, "n_claims": 3, "anchor": "videorft_incentivizing_video_reasoning_c", "bucket": "a"}
